ver on foot.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-21-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6014011","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"49aae3e825b6525e55c9f8d44f31fb31c79318769cf5d3759acd7c948118f218","compact":"b634e3297a434725c8233916cf4aaa758b9cf5ce75f9dd5e2f4e78a15af1b884","nasal":"b634e3297a434725c8233916cf4aaa758b9cf5ce75f9dd5e2f4e78a15af1b884"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-14-12","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":14,"verse":12,"english":"This abode of Makaras take me, who is forbearing, to be incompetent. Fie forbearance towards such as he! In consequence of my moderation, Ocean show not his own form. O Saumitri, bring you my bow, my arrows resembling venomous snakes. I will dry up the Ocean, and the monkeys shall go over on foot. Being angered, today, albeit incapable of being agitated, will I agitate the deep. And by means of my shafts will I make Varuna's abode, surging with a thousand billows and having his dignity maintained by his shores, overleep his continents. And I will agitate the deep harbouring numbers of mighty Dānavas.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.58,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-21-11","DUTT-6-21-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6014012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"32769609ddcfcacac504843110315688237ef43b458c6241e3e551993967451a","compact":"904eb7c5b4e00eede3ab74e2d36ec02601e541206274f87997e38abb5e72548c","nasal":"904eb7c5b4e00eede3ab74e2d36ec02601e541206274f87997e38abb5e72548c"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-14-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":14,"verse":13,"english":"Being angered, today, albeit incapable of being agitated, will I agitate the deep. And by means of my shafts will I make Varuna's abode, surging with a thousand billows and having his dignity maintained by his shores, overleep his continents. And I will agitate the deep harbouring numbers of mighty Dānavas.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-21-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6014013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"77ec05d344713a212e15112220c941a86b5abf1484371561f82afc9bb474cab8","compact":"975a78a32510c00b96b1a8d561b0d95392d51fe91340545b995019ee745b9c25","nasal":"975a78a32510c00b96b1a8d561b0d95392d51fe91340545b995019ee745b9c25"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-14-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":14,"verse":14,"english":"Having spoken you, Rāma, equipped with his bow, with his eyes dilated in wrath, became exceedingly irrepressible, like to the flaming fire at the final dissolution.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-21-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6014014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"17153651870dc66d2225c7601efcef53757cf4cb40ce6630f32c4a04313aef53","compact":"573bc9ff5f8fbac923062e0514d1cbf956eab5537ed0392ed81d4225de87882b","nasal":"fb34f0dd24539e3defb0a0b33af2c92d44a2c6da42be42775b153beb0b20b01f"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-14-15","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":14,"verse":15,"english":"And straining his dreadful bow, making the earth shake, tremulously, he let fly fierce shafts like him of an hundred sacrifices hurling his thunder-bolt.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.688,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-21-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6014015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9d4b36ae4f2700ed5b41372564282e1d9a42ac8f9b68859844b8e1a5addeb9ac","compact":"22e5390a86ed574153e0b2cd8e3e841708886f57ed2e36d2e93cc4df1798835a","nasal":"02dfa53ec965cbc8567e604c8e5d2b55ca731a4d4cef5fa1a22d9a2dd9684f76"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-14-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":14,"verse":16,"english":"Thereat, flaming up, those vehement choice shafts surcharged with energy, enter into the waters of the sea, with its serpents afflicted with fear.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.815,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-21-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6014016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"09d515b33e83463dfde2b28ca8cd9223de0efab22370523afab486770aca8bb7","compact":"96bb74bb97d6c1331acb1279875de981a8979403d98d23652b62d8beeb90c5bd","nasal":"c07030dceebaaaa792476fb20593cd9309472131be88e9baf280625ee460108a"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-14-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":14,"verse":17,"english":"Then great and exceedingly dreadful was the motion of the sea, with fishes and Makaras, and with the roar of the winds (blowing there).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.51,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-21-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6014017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5d53cc82554eb0f302db640b00a0b02ef1d50849e84856b1f828bd7c640ea5a2","compact":"7842c9a27bf594c77b4f057a516029b1fde7c4f9c039e45e40a2f759296cc234","nasal":"7842c9a27bf594c77b4f057a516029b1fde7c4f9c039e45e40a2f759296cc234"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-14-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":14,"verse":18,"english":"On a sudden the mighty deep was heaving with mighty surges, with conchs scattered about, and a smoke (enveloped) the ocean; and the billows became visible on all sides.","alignment":{"type":"approximate","confidence":0.22,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-21-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6014018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c84123